  "paper": "light-quanta",
  "argument": "arg-lq-fixed-band-volume",
  "title": "The entropy depends on the volume through a logarithm",
  "spoken": "The entropy difference is E over B frequency times the natural logarithm of the volume ratio.",
  "explanation": "At the same energy and band, the radiation's entropy in volume V exceeds that in V₀ by E over Bν times the logarithm of their ratio. Doubling the volume adds (E/Bν) ln 2, and doubling it again adds the same.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "Radiation of fixed energy E in a narrow band of frequencies around ν, compared in two volumes V and V₀.",
    "The Wien regime, with the integration constant of the entropy density set to zero.",
    "These are modern teaching equations in SI notation; the paper writes L for c, R/N for Boltzmann's constant, and β for B."
  ],
